$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-(4-Methylphenylsulfonyl)-iminophenyl-λ3-iodane 1 (34 mg, 0.090 mmol)
was added to a solution of carboxamide 2 (0.075 mmol) in dichloromethane
(1.5 mL) under stirring at room temperature. A change of the initially
heterogeneous mixture to a homogeneous solution was observed after
several minutes. The reaction mixture was stirred for 0.5-4 h (see Table
2), methanol (1.52 mL) was added, and stirring was continued for
additional 4.5 h at room temperature. Then the reaction mixture was
concentrated and separated by preparative TLC (hexane-ethyl acetate, 2: 1
or 3: 1). Methyl N-Pentylcarbamate (4s). Reaction of hexanamide 2s (9 mg,
0.075 mmol) according to the general procedure afforded 10 mg (92%) of
product 4s, isolated as a colorless oil. Time (h): 1. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 4.62 (br s, 1H), 3.66 (s, 3H), 3.22-3.06 (m, 2H), 1.49 (quint, J
= 7 Hz, 2H), 1.38-1.24 (m, 4H), 0.90 (t, J = 7 Hz, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM (Tosylimino)phenyl-λ3-iodane as a reagent for the synthesis of methyl
carbamates via Hofmann rearrangement of aromatic and aliphatic
carboxamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yoshimura, Akira; Luedtke, Matthew W.; Zhdankin, Viktor V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2012), 77(4), 2087-2091

