$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of benzylamine hydrochloride 3·HCl
from 2-phenylacetamide 2 via Hofmann rearrangement. To a mixture of
Oxone® (1.23 g, 2 mmol) and iodobenzene (0.204 g, 1 mmol) in CH3CN/H2O (6
mL, 1:1, v/v), 2-phenylacetamide 2 (0.135 g, 1 mmol) was added under
stirring at room temperature. The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 7 h (the reaction was monitored by GC-MS). After
completion of the reaction, the reaction mixture was filtered under
reduced pressure. The insoluble residue (mainly containing inorganic
salts) was washed with CH3CN (5 mL) and discarded. The combined filtrate
was mixed with HCl (15 mL, 20% aqueous solution), and the mixture was
washed with ether (10 mL) to remove all non-polar impurities. The aqueous
layer was concentrated at reduced pressure to give a sticky solid, which
was thoroughly dried in vacuum. Crystallization from ethanol-ether of
benzylamine hydrochloride 3·HCl as a slightly yellow crystalline solid.
Benzylamine hydrochloride 3·HCl from 2-phenylacetamide 2. 0.136 g (95%).
mp 253-255 °C (lit.1, mp 258-260 °C). 1H NMR 300 MHz (CD3OD): δ 4.12 (br
s, 2H,-CH2-), 7.40-7.48 (m, 5H, Ph).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hofmann rearrangement;
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hofmann Rearrangement of Carboxamides Mediated by Hypervalent Iodine
Species Generated in Situ from Iodobenzene and Oxone: Reaction Scope and
Limitations
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zagulyaeva, Aleksandra A.; Banek, Christopher T.; Yusubov, Mekhman S.;
Zhdankin, Viktor V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(20), 4644-4647

