$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A typical procedure is as follows: To a reddish orange suspension of
cyclohexanecarboxamide 1e (105 mg, 0.826 mmol), NBS (168 mg, 0.909 mmol)
and HgO (201 mg, 0.909 mmol) in 4 m/ of DMF, MeOH (334 mg 8.26 mmol) was
added at room temperature under argon. The reddish orange suspension was
stirred at room temperature for 0.5 hours, when it became orange.
Stirring of the mixture was allowed to continue for 11.5 hours to give a
whitish yellow suspension and it was filtered to eliminate BrHgOH. The
filtrate was diluted with 100 m/ of EtOAc, washed successively with H2O
(10 ml), 5% HCl (10 m/), H2O (10 m/), sat. NaHCO3 (10 m/) H2O (10 m/),
and brine (10 m/); dried over anhyd. MgSO4; and evaporated to give white
solid. This was purified by silica gel column chromatography (hexane:
EtOAc = 5:1). Colorless needles, yield 130 mg, 100%. mp. 74-75°C.
