$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Hofmann
Rearrangement. Amide (1 mmol) was added to the homogeneous solution of
methanol (50 mL) and KOH (2.5 mmol), and subsequently
(diacetoxyiodo)arene (1 mmol) was added to the solution. The mixture was
stirred for 15 min at 0 °C and then for 1 h at room temperature under
argon atmosphere. Then, the reaction mixture was evaporated, and the
residue was treated with pTLC on silica gel (eluent: hexane: ethyl
acetate = 3:1). methyl (E)-N-(2-phenylethenyl)carbamate, yield 98%. mp
115-116 °C (mp119 °C).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation and Reactivities of Novel (Diacetoxyiodo)arenes Bearing
Heteroaromatics
