$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Example 7: Preparation of
{(S)-4-methyl-2-[((S)-1-phenylethylcarbamoyl)-methyl]pentyl} carbamic
acid methyl ester (compound 4) A three-necked flask equipped with an
addition funnel, thermometer pocket, drying tube and a mechanical
stirrer, was charged with methanol (2000 ml), (R)-3-isobutylpentanedioic
acid amide-((S)-1-phenylmethyl) amide, compound of formula 1 (200 g,
0.689 mole) and cooled to 0° to 5°C followed by addition of sodium
methoxide (149 g, 2.758 mole). The reaction mass was cooled to −15 to
−25°C followed by addition of bromine (165.5 g, 1.034 mole) and stirred
for 1-2 h at −15 to −25°C. The mixture was gradually warmed to a
temperature of 0°C and then to 55-65°C, followed by stirring for 1 to 2
hours. The solvent was then stripped off and water was added to the mass.
The resulted slurry was further extracted with toluene, toluene layer
washed with brine followed by stripping off the solvent results in 215 g
(97% yield) of
{(S)-4-methyl-2-[((S)-1-phenylethylcarbamoyl)-methyl]pentyl} carbamic
acid methyl ester (4) with a purity of 90.9% area, as measured by HPLC.
