$DATUM Methyl 1-(benzyloxyimino)-2-methyl-4-phenylbutylcarbamate (6) A solution
of KOH (15 mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5 equiv.) in MeOH (0.6 ml) was added to amide
(30) (31 mg, 0.1 mmol, 1 equiv.) at RT. The resulting solution was cooled
to 0 °C (ice-bath) and PhI(OAc)2 (33 mg, 0.1 mmol, 1 equiv.) was added.
The mixture was stirred 15 min. at 0 °C and the 30 min. at RT. After
removal of the solvent under reduced pressure the residue was dissolved
in CH2Cl2 (15 ml) and washed with water (5 ml) and brine (5 ml). Drying
over Na2SO4 and removal of the solvent under reduced pressure afforded
the crude product, which was purified by flash chromatography
(hexane:EtOAc=4:1) to give methyl
1-(benzyloxyimino)-2-methyl-4-phenylbutylcarbamate (6) (31.9 mg, 94 %) as
colorless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.77 (bs, 1H, NH), 7.38-7.13 (m,
10H), 5.06 (d, 1H, 2 J=12 Hz, OCHA), 5.03 (d, 1H, 2 J=11.6 Hz, OCHB),
3.70 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.52-3.44 (m, 1H), 2.67-2.55 (m, 2H), 2.10-2.00 (m,
1H), 1.73-1.63 (m, 1H), 1.22 (d, 3H, 3 J=6.8 Hz, CH3); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
101 MHz) δ 151.83, 151.44, 142.60, 137.49, 128.44, 128.38, 128.37,
128.22, 128.00, 125.62, 75.90, 52.46, 35.81, 33.44, 33.11, 18.36; IR ν
3405 (w), 3064 (w), 3028 (w), 2934 (w), 1754 (s), 1635 (s), 1481 (s),
1455 (m), 1385 (w), 1364 (w), 1273 (w), 1212 (s), 1097 (w), 1079 (w),
1035 (m), 926 (w), 881 (w), 770 (w), 750 (m), 698 (s), 628 (w); HRMS
(EI): calcd for C20H24N2O3 + (M) 340.1782 Found 340.1781
