$DATUM [0274] Example 14 Method for producing (R)-1-(p-chlorobenzoyl)-3-amino
piperidine [0276] To the white crystal (5.7 g) obtained in Example 11,
water (30 ml), sodium hydroxide (1.7 g, 2 equivalents) and aqueous sodium
hypochlorite solutions (13.4 g, 1 equivalent) were added. The mixture was
stirred at 15 to 40 °C for 2 hours to obtain a pale yellow aqueous
solution (54.1 g). To 10.3 g of the subdivided solution, isopropanol (5
ml) and sodium chloride (1 g) were added. The mixture was stirred at 60°
C. for 10 minutes. The water layer was removed and the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure to obtain the title compound as yellow
oil (0.87 g, yield: 90%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hofmann rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Method for producing optically active 3-aminopiperidine or salt thereof
