$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 5-Methyl-2-Oxazolidinone To the suspension of
3-hydroxyamide (1.00 g, 9.70 mmol) and AgOAc (1.94 g, 11.6 mmol) in 10 ml
of acetonitrile, the NBS (2.02 g, 11.6 mmol) solution in 30 ml of
acetonitrile was added at 0 °C under Ar atmosphere, then stirred for 2
hrs at 0 °C and 10 hrs at room temperature. After 12 hrs acetonitrile was
evaporated; extracted with 300 ml of ethylacetate; washed with 10% Na2CO3
(30 ml• 5% HCl (30 mlx2), H2O (30 mlx1) and sat. NaCl (30 mlx2); dried
over anhydrous MgSO4 and evaporated to give 1.02 g of oil, then purified
with column chromatography (EtOAc). 1,3-Oxazine-2-one 4-hydroxybutanamide
(1.00 g, 9.70 mmol), AgOAc (1.94 g, 11.6 mmol), NBS (1.72 g, 11.6 mmol);
yield 890 mg, 90%. mp: 82-84 °C IR(nujol) cm-1: 3250, 1680; 1H-NMR
(CDCl3) δ : 1.10-1.75 (m, 2H, CH2), 3.05-3.30 (m, 2H, CH2N), 3.40-3.80
(m, 2H, CH2O), 4.30-4.70 (br, 1H, NH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A facile synthetic method of 2-oxazolidinones and 1,3-oxazine-2-ones,
essential moieties of a new antiulcer agent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Park, Min Soo; Lee, Jae Won
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Archives of Pharmacal Research (1993), 16(2), 158-60

