$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
t,t-2,6-Diacetoxy-r-1-tert-butoxycarbonylaminio-1-cyanocyclohexane (3a):
Pb(OAc)4 (20 g) was added to a solution of 2b (2.5 g, 9.32 mmol) in
t-BuOH/DMF (40:10mL). The mixture was stirred and boiled under reflux for
40 min, and then cooled. Toluene (100 mL) and Et2O (50 mL) were added and
the solution was filtered, washed with H2O (2 x 50 mL), dried (Na2SO4)
and concentrated. The crude was purified by column chromatography
(Et2O/hexane, 5:1) to give 3a.
t,t-3,5-Diacetoxy-r-4-tert-butoxycarbonylamino-4-cyanotetrahydropyran
(3b): Using the same amounts and conditions as described of 2b, except
that a reaction time of 0.5 h was used, compound 2c6 gave 3b (2.62g,
87.7%). mp 123-124°C. C15H22N2O7(354.4), calc.found: C 52.63,52.26 H
6.48, 6.52 N 8.18, 8.18; IR: ν = 3343, 1737, 1645, 1522 cm-1. 1H NMR
(CDCl3/TMS): δ = 1.43 [s, 9H, (CH3)3C], 2.14 (s, 6H, 2Ac), 3.94 (dd, 2H,
J = 12.1, 4.5Hz, H-2e, 6e), 3.62 (dd, 2H, J = 12.1, 9.3 Hz, H-2a, 6a),
5.27 (br s, 1 H, NH), 5.34 (dd, 2H, J = 9.3, 4.5 Hz, H-3,5). 13C NMR
(CDCl3/TMS): δ = 20.8 (2 CH3CO), 28.8 [(CH3)3C], 60.1 (C-4), 66.0
(C-2,6), 68.5 (C-3,5), 113.9 (CN), 153.0 (CONH), 169.9 (2CO).
