$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM p-Isocyanatotoluene (3a).
N-(4-Methylphenylsulfonyl)-iminophenyl-λ3-iodane 1 (34 mg, 0.09 mmol) was
added to a solution of p-toluamide 2a (10 mg, 0.075 mmol) in
dichloromethane (1.5 mL) and stirred at room temperature for 0.5 h. After
completion of the reaction, the mixture was concentrated and separated by
preparative TLC (hexane-ethyl acetate = 2: 1) to afford final product.
The obtained product is identical to a commercially available sample. 8
mg (80%), isolated as a brown oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.22 (d, J =
8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.14 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 2.33 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM (Tosylimino)phenyl-λ3-iodane as a reagent for the synthesis of methyl
carbamates via Hofmann rearrangement of aromatic and aliphatic
carboxamides
