$DATUM 87-90-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):RGT(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 6674-22-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 1-(methoxycarbonylamino)-2-vinylcyclopropanecarboxylate (8). A 22
L flask was charged with
(1R,2R)-methyl-1-carbamoyl-2-vinylcyclopropanecarboxylate (270 g,1.60
mol), methanol (10 volumes, 2.7 liters) and DBU (541 ml, 3.59 mol), and
then cooled in an ice bath to below 12 °C. trichloroisocyanuric acid (130
g, 559 mmol)(TCCA) was then added in approximately 5 g portions over a
period of about 45 minutes, maintaining an internal temperature below 15
°C. After the addition was complete, the ice bath was removed, and the
reaction was allowed to warm to 26 °C (1 h). The reaction was incomplete
by TLC so additional TCCA (15 g) was added in four portions at 26 °C. By
TLC the intermediate formation was complete. The reaction was then heated
to refluxand monitored by TLC. After 2.5 h, none of the N-chloro
intermediate was observed, and the reaction was cooled to room
temperature and worked up. The reaction was concentrated on a rotovap to
an oil containing a precipitate, then taken up in EtOAc (2.4 L) and
washed successively with NaOH (1 N, 1.5 L), HCl (1N, 1.5 L) and brine
(200 ml). The NaOH layer was back extracted with 750 mL EtOAc, and the
same EtOAc solution was used to back extract the HCl and brine layers.
The organic layers were combined and concentrated at reduced pressure to
provide the crude product as an amber oil, yield 246 g, 77%. TLC (1:1
hexanes / EtOAc, stain withanisaldehyde, rf = 0.8). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 1.55 (s, 1H), 1.84 (t, J = 6 Hz,1H), 2.19 (q, J = 17.6, 8.8 Hz,
1H), 3.70 (s, 3H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 5.15 (dd, J = 10, 1.2 Hz,1H), 5.32 (m,
2H), 5.75 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 171.3, 157.0, 133.6,
118.2, 52.6, 40.9, 34.7, 23.6. IR (cm-1): 1728, 1603. HRMS calcd for
C9H13NO4 (M + 1): 200.0917, found 200.0917.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hoffman rearrangement, MeOH also used as solvent, slow addition of
trichloroisocyanuric acid with temperature control, using excess oxidant
should be avoided, scalable (246 g scale)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of
methyl-1-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)-2-vinylcyclopropanecarboxylate via a
Hofmann rearrangement utilizing trichloroisocyanuric acid as an oxidant
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Crane, Zackary D.; Nichols, Paul J.; Sammakia, Tarek; Stengel, Peter J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2011), 76(1), 277-280

