$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-(tert-Butoxycarbonylamino)-2-deoxypyranosides 3; General
Procedure: Method C: (for 3a-c): Glycoside 1 a-c (0.5 mmol) is dissolved
in a mixture of t-BuOH (10 mL) and DMF (5mL). Subsequently Pb(OAc)4 (1.1
g, 2.5 mmol) is added and the mixture is stirred and refluxed for 3 h.
Solvents arc removed in vacuo, and the residue is chromatographed on a
silica gel column (10x2 cm) using hexane/Et2O (7:3) as an eluant to give
3 a-c. Compound 3c, yield 74%. mp(°C)b (solvent) 181-182 (benzene/Hx) [α
]D (c,CHCl3) ±8.8 (1.0) Molecular Formulac C25H33NO6 (443.5) IR ν (cm-1)
1705 1H-NMR (solvent/TMS, 500 MHz)d δ , J(Hz) (C6D6, 70°C): 1.42 (s, 9H,
C(CH3)3), 3.17 (dd, 1H, J4,5 = 2.5, J5,5' = 11.8, H-5), 3.26 (s, 3 H,
OCH3), 3.42 (m, 1 H, J4,5 = 5.5, J3,4 = 3.1, H-4), 3.95 (brm, 1H, H-3),
3.98 (dt, 1H, J1,2 = 5.1, J2,3 = 7.8, H-2), 4.00 (dd, 1H, H-5'), 4.50
(brd, 1H, H-1)
