$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 6a: To a stirred solution of 5a
(0.10 g, 0.48 mmol) in CH3CN-H2O (2 mL, 1:1 v/v), PhI(CF3CO2)2 (0.25 g,
0.58 mmol) was added at room temperature. After stirring for 1 h, it was
cooled to 0 °C and Et3N (0.27 mL, 1.93 mmol), followed by Boc2O (0.20 mL,
0.96 mmol) were added and stirring was continued for 1 h at the same
temperature. The reaction mixture was then diluted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL),
washed with saturated NH4Cl (5 mL), brine (5 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by column chromatography (SiO2, 20%
EtOAc in petroleum ether as eluant) furnished 6a. Compound 6b, yield 70%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
