$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [0271] (Example 13) Method for producing (R)-1-(p-methylbenzoyl)-3-amino
piperidine [0273] To the white crystal (4.0 g) obtained in Example 11,
water (20 ml), sodium hydroxide (1.3 g, 2 equivalents) and aqueous sodium
hypochlorite solution (10.2 g, 1 equivalent) were added. The mixture was
stirred at 15 to 40 °C for 2 hours to obtain a pale yellow aqueous
solution (34.7 g). To 11.0 g of the subdivided solution, isopropanol (5
ml) and sodium chloride (1 g) were added. The mixture was stirred at 60
°C for 10 minutes. The water layer was separated and the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure to obtain the title compound as yellow
oil (0.72 g, yield: 64%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
