$DATUM 3-Amino-4,6-dimethyl-5-nitropyridine (4). Bromine (0.6 ml, 12 mmol) was
added dropwise to a solution of NaOH (1.5 g, 37.5 mmol) in water (16 ml)
at -5°C, then nicotinamide 3a [1] (1.5 g, 7.7 mmol) was added, stirred
with cooling for 30 min, then slowly heated to 75°C and kept at this
temperature for 2.5 h. The precipitate formed was filtered off, washed
with 10% HCl (20 ml), boiled with activated charcoal, cooled, neutralized
with aqueous ammonia, and the residue was recrystallized from toluene.
3-Amino-4,6-dimethyl-5-nitropyridine (4). Yield 63%. mp 173-174°C
(toluene). Found, %: C 50.12; H 5.32; N 24.98. C7H9N3O2. Calculated, %: C
50.29, H 5.43, N 25.14; IR spectrum, ν, cm-1:1370, 1530 (NO2), 3395, 3500
(NH2); 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz)*: 1.92 (3H, s, 4-CH3); 2.20 (3H,
s, 6-CH3); 5.55 (2H, s, NH2); 7.95 (1H, s, H-2); m/z (I ,%)*: 168 [M+1]+•
(9), 167 [M]+• (100), 150 (29), 121 (68), 120 (13), 119 (10), 95 (15), 94
(23), 93 (11), 81 (12), 80 (29), 67 (20), 66 (15), 65 (15), 54 (15), 53
(27), 42 (12), 39 (13).
