$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM [0327] (Example 33) Method for producing (R)-1-(benzyl)-3-amino
piperidine In (R)-1-(benzyl)nipecotamide (1.1 g) produced by the method
described in Example 2, water (5 ml), a 30% aqueous sodium hydroxide
solution (6.7 g, 10 equivalents), THF (10 ml), an aqueous sodium
hypochlorite solution (11.2 g, 1.5 equivalents) were mixed. The mixture
was stirred at 15° C for 1 hour and at 60 °C for 2 hours. The mixture was
cooled to 20 °C and extracted with toluene (10 ml) 3 times. After the
organic layers were combined, the combined organic layer was concentrated
under reduced pressure to obtain the title compound as yellowish brown
oil (0.8 g, yield: 55%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Method for producing optically active 3-aminopiperidine or salt thereof
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
